          "source_text_sha256": "e1daa9e01eb00239a4c90cb9eaf6541f5d52c998045ca29d6a49c57f4c00259b",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 14, 2013 at 3:00 AM, a driver observed a very fast passing in the sky of a silver fireball that disappeared towards the N-E. No other witnesses have come forward. The observation of a very bright fireball, crossing the sky in less than a second, suggests a bolide (large meteor) phenomenon caused by the atmospheric entry of a fragment of a comet, or asteroid. December 14 is a date during the peak activity of the Geminid meteor shower: the BOAM observer network recorded dozens of them that night. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a bolide, from the Geminid shower.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "acf96c57e574546efbeae66740821450058bb994e4faaa3dc8f5311f130f53a2"
        }
